    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[3]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/documents/guideline/guidelines-22023-on-technical-scope-of-art-53-of-eprivacy-directive_en"^^xsd:anyURI .

lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-p35-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-p35 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-03"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[3]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/documents/guideline/guidelines-22023-on-technical-scope-of-art-53-of-eprivacy-directive_en"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text "35. Storage of information in the sense of Article 5(3) ePD refers to placing information on a physical electronic storage medium that is part of a user or subscriber’s terminal equipment."@en .

lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-p37
    a lgo:Provision ;
    eli:is_part_of lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02 ;
    lgo:citation "EDPB Guidelines 2/2023, para. 37" ;
    lgo:interprets lg:EU-2002-58-art5-3 ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[3]/paragraph[2]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/documents/guideline/guidelines-22023-on-technical-scope-of-art-53-of-eprivacy-directive_en"^^xsd:anyURI .

lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-p37-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-p37 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-03"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[3]/paragraph[2]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/documents/guideline/guidelines-22023-on-technical-scope-of-art-53-of-eprivacy-directive_en"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text "37. The ePD does not place any upper or lower limit on the length of time that information must persist on a storage medium to be counted as stored, nor is there an upper or lower limit on the amount of information to be stored."@en .

lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-p50
    a lgo:Provision ;
    eli:is_part_of lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02 ;
    lgo:citation "EDPB Guidelines 2/2023, para. 50" ;
    lgo:interprets lg:EU-2002-58-art5-3 ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[4]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/documents/guideline/guidelines-22023-on-technical-scope-of-art-53-of-eprivacy-directive_en"^^xsd:anyURI .

lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-p50-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-p50 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-03"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[4]/paragraph[1]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/documents/guideline/guidelines-22023-on-technical-scope-of-art-53-of-eprivacy-directive_en"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text "50. Both tracking links and tracking pixels can be distributed through a wide variety of channels, for example through emails, web sites, or even, in the case of tracking links, through any kind of text messaging systems. That distribution to the user’s terminal equipment does constitute storage, at the very least through the caching mechanism of the client-side software. As such, Article 5(3) ePD is applicable, even if this storage is not permanent."@en .

lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-p51
    a lgo:Provision ;
    eli:is_part_of lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02 ;
    lgo:citation "EDPB Guidelines 2/2023, para. 51" ;
    lgo:interprets lg:EU-2002-58-art5-3 ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[4]/paragraph[2]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/documents/guideline/guidelines-22023-on-technical-scope-of-art-53-of-eprivacy-directive_en"^^xsd:anyURI .

lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-p51-q1
    a lgo:Quote ;
    lgo:officialLanguageVersion true ;
    lgo:quoteOf lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-p51 ;
    lgo:retrievedOn "2026-11-03"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceDocument lg:EDPB-GL-2023-02-source ;
    lgo:sourceElement "/law/section[4]/paragraph[2]" ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://www.edpb.europa.eu/documents/guideline/guidelines-22023-on-technical-scope-of-art-53-of-eprivacy-directive_en"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:text "51. The addition of tracking information to URLs or images (pixels) sent to the user constitutes an instruction to the terminal equipment to send back the targeted information (the specified identifier). In the case of dynamically constructed tracking pixels, it is the distribution of the applicative logic (usually a JavaScript code) that constitutes the instruction. As a consequence, it can be considered that the collection of identifiers provided through such tracking mechanisms constitutes a ‘gaining of access’ in the meaning of Article 5(3) ePD, thus it applies to that step as well."@en .

